"""PANEL BANK, part 2: (a) TRUE-vs-FALSE discrimination pairs, (b) contamination GATES. EN/DE/FR.

(a) TRUEFALSE — the adversarial test. Each item: (stem, true_outcome, false_outcome, neutral).
    The false twin is an equally dramatic, period-plausible counterfactual that did NOT happen.
    Score: calibrated preference c(true)-c(false) under the PRE model, c(a)=slp(stem,a)-slp(neutral,a).
    If the measure just rewards drama, pre-minds prefer true and false equally; if the pre-mind points
    at the RIGHT catastrophes, 'foreseeable in kind' becomes 'foreseeable in fact'.

(b) GATES — 6 post-event fact probes per event, 4-way forced choice, run under the event's PRE model.
    Facts are chosen to be UNKNOWABLE pre-event and (where possible) not guessable from pre-event
    priors. Years are digits (identically tokenized, length-matched options). A pre model at chance
    (25%) is GREEN: its low surprise is foresight, not leakage.
"""

